The spacing between neighboring momenta is $\Delta p=\frac{\hbar}{R}.$ As $R\to\infty$, this spacing tends to zero. A continuum-normalized momentum basis may be obtained by the same rescaling used for position: $\begin{aligned}
  \ket{p_n}_{\mathrm c}
  &:=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\Delta p}}\ket n,\\
  {}_{\mathrm c}\!\braket{p_m}{p_n}_{\mathrm c}
  &=\frac{\delta_{mn}}{\Delta p}\\
  &\longrightarrow\delta(p-p').\end{aligned}$

