Suppose a detector at the barrier records which opening the electron used. The detector must then become correlated with the alternative. Schematically, $\ket\Psi
    =\ket{\text{path }1}\ket{D_1}
     +\ket{\text{path }2}\ket{D_2}.$ When the detector records are distinguishable, the electron alone no longer has the same interference term. A full explanation requires composite systems and entanglement, so it belongs after the tensor-product structure has been developed.

